# Curated rekordbox master.db fixture for state-ingest tests.
# Source: a private live rekordbox library, pruned by
# scripts/make_rb_fixture.py (see that file for the pipeline).
#
# PRIVACY -- this is why the fixture is leaving the repo: the rows carry real
# track titles, provider track IDs and filesystem paths. It is private library
# data, not a
# credential, and it must not be published. See
# docs/oss-going-public-checklist.md blocker 2.
#
# Regenerable on a machine with the live library: python -m scripts.make_rb_fixture
#
# INERT UNTIL THE HISTORY REWRITE. _resolver.fixture_path() prefers a real
# directory (rule 1) over a marker (rule 2), so while tests/fixtures/rekordbox/
# is still committed this file changes nothing. It takes effect the moment the
# blob is stripped, which is the point: no flag day.
rekordbox
